WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.230
A murderer knocks at your door and
asks where your friend is hiding.

2
00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:10.090
In 1797, Immanuel Kant argued
that you may not lie, even then.

3
00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:13.340
Is Kantian ethics too rigid to be useful?

4
00:00:13.390 --> 00:00:17.500
You may know every fact about
Kant, and still not have an answer.

5
00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:21.380
Three essays, two hours, 120 marks.

6
00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:25.070
So what turns knowledge
into a 40-mark argument?

7
00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:28.500
In this mission, you'll put four
questions through two gates,

8
00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:30.020
and choose your three.

9
00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:32.790
Then you'll map an essay
on Kant as an argument,

10
00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:34.020
testing him against W.

11
00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:34.210
D.

12
00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:36.460
Ross and Christine Korsgaard.

13
00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:41.400
Your mission: find out what turns what
you know into a sustained argument.
